{"id":"chemosh","name":"Chemosh","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:chemosh"],"types":[{"type":"deity","from":"UBS: Names of Deities"}],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":["An idol of"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Chemosh","text":"The destroyer, subduer, or fish-god, the god of the Moabites (Num. 21:29; Jer. 48:7, 13, 46). The worship of this god, “the abomination of Moab,” was introduced at Jerusalem by Solomon (1 Kings 11:7), but was abolished by Josiah (2 Kings 23:13). On the “Moabite Stone” (q.v.), Mesha (2 Kings 3:5) ascribes his victories over the king of Israel to this god, “And Chemosh drove him before my sight.”"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3645","lemma":"כְּמוֹשׁ","xlit":"Kᵉmôwsh","gloss":"Kemosh, the god of the Moabites","kjv":"Chemosh","count":7,"share":1},{"strong":"H6440","lemma":"פָּנִים","xlit":"pânîym","gloss":"the face","kjv":"accept, a- fore, against, anger","count":3,"share":0.43},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":4,"share":0.57}],"verses":["Judg.11.24","1Kgs.11.7","1Kgs.11.33","2Kgs.23.13","Jer.48.7","Jer.48.13","Jer.48.46"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"moabites","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.023,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"baal-zephon","type":"lexical","strong":"H6440","why":"both lead with פָּנִים (H6440)"},{"id":"battle","type":"lexical","strong":"H6440","why":"both lead with פָּנִים (H6440)"},{"id":"countenance","type":"lexical","strong":"H6440","why":"both lead with פָּנִים (H6440)"},{"id":"footman","type":"lexical","strong":"H6440","why":"both lead with פָּנִים (H6440)"},{"id":"girgashites","type":"lexical","strong":"H6440","why":"both lead with פָּנִים (H6440)"},{"id":"jeshimon","type":"lexical","strong":"H6440","why":"both lead with פָּנִים (H6440)"}],"works":[{"work":"philo","tit